{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be your doctor during this stay. You're here because of nausea and vomiting. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up the morning of admission feeling really nauseous. I started vomiting and couldn’t keep anything down. I’ve had this before with my gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right, I see you have Type 1 diabetes and a gastric pacer for gastroparesis. You had a Botox injection recently too. Any pain, fever, or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No pain, no fever. Just the nausea and vomiting. I did notice some dark stuff in the vomit—was that blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. It could be a small tear from vomiting, called a Mallory-Weiss tear. We’ll watch that. In the ER, they placed a nasogastric tube to help with the nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I pulled it out later. It was uncomfortable and I thought I was feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. We’ll monitor you closely. You’re on IV fluids and anti-nausea meds like Zofran and Reglan. We also gave Ativan to help you rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Is my blood pressure okay? I know it’s been high before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was elevated at 169/94 when you arrived. We’re managing it with IV metoprolol if needed. Once you can take pills, we’ll restart your lisinopril."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my sugar? I’m worried about that too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose was 236 earlier, which is high, but expected since you’re under stress. We’re giving insulin glargine at night and adjusting as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on fluconazole for a yeast infection in my esophagus. Should I keep taking that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you completed the course before coming in. The EGD last time showed candidiasis, but the biopsy didn’t confirm fungus. Still, we’ll assume it’s treated for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my gastric pacer—was that checked?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, an X-ray confirmed it’s in the right place. The leads are stable. The NG tube was also confirmed in the stomach, though one part was a bit high at first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s working okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The device is fine. But your stomach isn’t emptying well, which is why you’re vomiting. This flare-up may be related to your diabetes control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been trying to manage it. The Botox helped for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-01-19 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can wear off. We’re not doing another procedure this time. We’ll treat this flare with bowel rest and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m back to check on you. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I haven’t vomited since this morning. Still a little nauseous, but not as bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. We repeated some labs. Your hemoglobin is stable, around 10.7 to 11.8. No sign of ongoing bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the dark vomit? Was that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it was a small tear from vomiting. It usually heals on its own. Your hemoglobin didn’t drop, so no transfusion is needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my acid levels? I saw something about acidosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your bicarbonate was a bit low at 21, which means mild metabolic acidosis. It’s likely from not eating and vomiting. It’s improving with fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. When can I start eating again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-01-19 18:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll try small sips tomorrow. If you tolerate that, we’ll advance to clear liquids, then soft foods. We don’t want to trigger vomiting again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-01-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Ready to try some water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-01-20 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel okay. No nausea right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-01-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Start with a few sips. We’ll wait 30 minutes to see how you do. Your blood sugar was 187 this morning—still high, but manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-01-20 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You kept the water down. That’s a good sign. We’ll give you more and add some broth later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-01-20 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried I’d never be able to eat again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-01-20 09:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most patients improve with time. We’re also continuing your pantoprazole for GERD and gastritis. It helps protect your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-01-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well—clear liquids, then a soft diet. No vomiting. How’s your energy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-01-21 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still tired, but I walked in the hall this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-01-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Your labs are stable. Hemoglobin is 11.8, glucose is 225—still high, but you’re on your usual insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-01-21 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I adjust my Humalog?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-01-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re following your home sliding scale. We’ll keep that plan. Your diabetes is uncontrolled right now, but we’re working on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-01-22 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. You’ve been on a soft diet all day with no issues. We’re thinking about discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-01-22 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. Will my meds change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-01-22 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not much. You’ll keep lisinopril for blood pressure, pantoprazole once daily instead of twice, and your insulin as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-01-22 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on Zofran as needed. Should I keep that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-01-22 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll send you home with it. Use it if nausea returns. But call your GI doctor if it happens often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-01-22 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the iron deficiency? I’ve had that for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-01-22 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your anemia is stable. It’s likely from chronic issues, including iron deficiency. We don’t need to treat it now, but your doctor may check iron levels later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home today. You’ve been off IVs, eating well, and feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Start with small, frequent meals. Avoid large portions. Keep taking your meds. Follow up with GI and your primary doctor in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll make sure to do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call us if you start vomiting again or can’t keep food down. Otherwise, take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—your ECG showed sinus tachycardia, which is common with dehydration and stress. It’s improved, so no concern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried about that. Glad it’s not serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s expected. Just focus on staying hydrated and eating small meals. You’ve done really well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try my best. The Botox helped before—should I consider it again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Discuss that with your GI doctor. It’s an option if symptoms return. For now, let’s see how you do with diet and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ll follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You can leave once the nurse reviews everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2198-01-23 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and feel better soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-01-19 13:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-01-23 13:55:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis s/p gastric pacer presented with acute nausea and vomiting, one week after a prior hospitalization for similar symptoms. She had recently received a Botox injection for gastroparesis and noticed dark material in her vomit, likely due to a Mallory-Weiss tear. She was admitted for inability to tolerate oral intake and managed with bowel rest, IV fluids, and antiemetics including Zofran, Reglan, and Ativan. A nasogastric tube was placed in the ED but removed by the patient. Her symptoms improved gradually, allowing advancement to a soft diet. Labs showed mild metabolic acidosis and stable hemoglobin, with no evidence of ongoing bleeding. She was discharged home in stable condition on her prior medications with follow-up planned in gastroenterology and primary care.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroesophageal laceration-hemorrhage syndrome",
      "Acute posthemorrhagic anemia",
      "Acidosis",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Benign essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux"
    ]
  }
}
